 @dhaumyagango1076  I said I have the exact same settings my 3080 Ti IS performing similar since part of the setup is the frame limiter or rather the vsync which auto locks your fps to the hz rate of your monitor. How many frames his hardware would put out without a locked frame rate, we will maybe never know, but at those settings, the settings that I am using too, it is 60 frames at 4k. The same frame rate that I have. And probably a lot of other people too with a 3080ti.
And yes, I said that the dlss has to activated to maintain the 60 fps, which is also true for both cards. Because turning off the dlss drops performance for me to about 50 percent and I'm guessing it's similar for the 3090Ti. That would leave you with 30 frames for my hardware and about 33 frames for his. Has nothing to do with locked fps but makes the same point: Same settings, same results. Dlss turned off = no 60 fps.
Anymore questions? And please read carefully before you reply again and maybe ask a friend because your reading comprehension doesn't seem to be the best. Thank you.
